# One owner per service: li-915 § Ownership (staged for op-316 item 8,
# /Users/me/wip-mach/stage/op316-input/li-915-ownership.md, sha256 c58aa32f...).
# The boot check asserts it: no service both in `service -e` and in
# `launchctl list`, and every launchd job below loaded.
#
# The loader (/boot/loader.conf, sealed base) owns the kernel, modules, root
# selection and console; an owner's kernel settings live on the ESP's
# loader.env, written by the installer. softwareupdate never writes either.
#
# launchd <label> [<rc service the job replaces> ...]
launchd	org.rmxos.logd	syslogd asld
launchd	org.rmxos.logd-retention.once
launchd	com.apple.notifyd
launchd	com.rmxos.console-getty
launchd	org.rmxos.softwareupdate.boot-check
#
# rc <service>: the machine (rc.conf on Data, vendor.conf in the base).
rc	netif
rc	routing
rc	sshd
rc	zfs
rc	dumpon
rc	powerd
rc	random
